WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.580
A window ledge.

2
00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:04.820
Three names, scratched into the paint.

3
00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:06.430
Catherine Earnshaw.

4
00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.030
Catherine Heathcliff.

5
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:09.660
Catherine Linton.

6
00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:14.740
Across the moor stand two houses:
a low, windswept farmhouse,

7
00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:18.270
and a great house in a
park, its windows lit.

8
00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:21.020
A wild girl crosses from one to the other,

9
00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:23.370
and comes back in a riding habit.

10
00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.370
Later she cries, "Nelly, I am Heathcliff!"

11
00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.800
So why does she marry Edgar?

12
00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:32.650
In this mission, you'll
compare the two houses,

13
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.740
and what each one offers her.

14
00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:38.140
You'll hear Catherine give
her reasons, in her own words.

15
00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:41.150
And you'll ask what a wedding
did to a woman's property,

16
00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.970
before the law changed in 1870.

17
00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:47.410
Your mission: explain
why she marries Edgar.
